WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Last time you did our show,
we were --

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the one week
we went afield of New York.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:04.704 line:92%
We went to Washington, D.C.,

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
and performed in the giant
Warner Theatre.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.341
-Beautiful theater.
-And you said you were going to

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:11.344
have a very hard time coming
back to this little theater.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.213 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How is it so far?

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's fine.
-Okay.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you for being honest.
-You're welcome.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what?
I have to pee so bad.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:22.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I decided
I'm not going to do it.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to use it.
-Oh.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because we're artists.
-Yeah.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it's really distracting.
-Oh, wow.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:30.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, now looking back, you made
a mistake, would you say?

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.400 size:84% position:42%
-I feel like I probably
should have done it.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.634 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It does only get worse.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Famously.
Yeah. It doesn't pass.

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm not going to, like,
stop things to pee. I'm fine.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:44.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you had some kind of
wide-mouthed Snapple bottle,

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:46.379 line:92%
I would do it right here.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.881 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I don't. I don't.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:51.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Anyway, go see
this children's movie.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-Sorry.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.254 line:92%
-Because I've heard you --

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.189 size:78% position:39%
Obviously you have to
promote this movie

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is a wonderful movie
for children,

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.559 size:75% position:38%
even though it deals
with serious themes.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you were warned
during the first press tour

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.532 size:84% position:42%
to remember that it was
a film for children.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:09.869 size:88% position:44%
-Well, "Wreck-It Ralph,"
that was the first one.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.104 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.139 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.707 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Kidding, kidding.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:18.111 line:92%
So then we started promoting it.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:22.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one day,
we went to Disneyland.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we did a bunch --
It was a junket.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:28.021 size:81% position:41%
It wasn't like we were
at Soarin', you know?

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:31.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they take us
from room to room to room

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
to do junket interviews
with people.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they kept drilling it
into me, you know,

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
just a reminder that
this is a children's movie

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
and blah, blah, blah,
and I'm like, "I get it.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:44.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not, you know,
a monster or whatever."

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.472 line:92%
And so I do the first interview,

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:49.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then they're walking me
to the next interview.

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
And on the walk,
the woman was like,

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:55.515
"Just want to remind you again,
it is a children's movie."

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:58.418
And I go, "You know what?
This is honestly insulting.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a grown woman.
I certainly know the --

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.823 line:92%
Yes, I work blue in my comedy,

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I certainly
know the difference."

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:06.726 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And she goes, "Well,

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:10.396
in that interview, you just
said that Q-bert does coke."

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:15.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "I did?
I have no memory of that."

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.470 line:92%
-It would make sense, though.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It would make so much sense.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:22.709
He looks -- I feel like he's
built for it, Q-bert, right?

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:26.746
Doesn't Q-bert have -- Isn't he
just all just one long nose?

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:29.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. He's one long nose.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:33.553
-And then he's constantly
talking in inaudible...

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:37.090 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:40.226
This movie is --
You go from the video-game world

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the world of the Internet.
-Yeah.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:44.497
-And it actually tackles themes
of the Internet in a way

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.966
that I think will be really
interesting for kids to see

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it is a wonderful place,
the Internet,

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also a terrifying place.
-100%.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.405 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And it's nice to reflect

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
the world that they
actually live in.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:56.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I mean, it's the Internet,
good and bad.

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.344 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's bombardment.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:02.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
It builds you up.
It crushes you down.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:07.620
And you start pinning your worth
on outside things.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the only way to survive it
is to kind of look inward,

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:12.792 line:92%
which is not just for kids,

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:16.896
but something that we all kind
of constantly need to learn.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:19.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the bad guy in it
is not a bad guy.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just Ralph's
own insecurity.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
It really -- I know
it's just a Disney movie.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's about
the human condition.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:29.275
But I will admit, that's what
I've been saying in press.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.678
And, really, you could just
say that about anything.

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:33.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everything's about
the human condition.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.482 size:78% position:39%
It just sounds smart.
It sounds very smart.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:37.850 line:92%
-On the Internet, you have

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
experienced both
the good and the bad.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.521 size:81% position:41%
I have always found it
incredibly commendable

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
and have been very impressed
with the fact

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:47.060
that sometimes you, when people
maybe will come at you

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
with negativity,
instead of blocking them,

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:52.298 size:84% position:42%
you engage with them
with a level of empathy

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
that not a lot of people use
as a tool.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:57.971
-I don't always do it.
It's a -- You know, I'm trying.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:00.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not always my best self,
you know?

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But, yeah.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I feel like
it's a vulnerable --

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:06.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
To me, I see a big difference
between the liars

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.249 line:92%
who I have no respect, patience,

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:12.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
and don't feel
I need to be open to...

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:18.057
and the lied-to,
whose crime is believing liars.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:21.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure. Well, your show --
Your fantastic show on Hulu.

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:22.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I Love You, America."
-Nice.

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously you used --
Congratulations.

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:25.798 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
You use that, as well.
-Yeah.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because now that wall
of social media

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.539
where you actually can't look
people in the eye is gone.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:36.042
And have you found it rewarding
to talk to people that,

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:40.647
from the get-go, obviously have
a different worldview than you?

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:41.047 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hugely.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I had a family dinner
with a family in Wyoming,

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:46.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're conservative
Republicans.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:50.723 size:81% position:41%
And, you know, I think
when I'm flying there

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're anticipating me,
we're filling our brains.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:54.827 line:92%
Your brain, like, fills in

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.897
what you don't know with
something that you do know.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's not accurate
until you're there, you know?

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:06.239
And I don't think we changed
each other's minds at all.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:09.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we --
I left there loving them.

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.076 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You know what I mean?

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:13.346
You go to Thanksgiving, and half
the people you don't agree with.

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.315 line:92%
-Yeah. This is very exciting.

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:16.949 line:92%
We've talked about this before.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:17.950 line:92%
We're from the same hometown,

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.719 size:84% position:42%
a little place called
Bedford, New Hampshire.

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:21.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a dear friend
of my mother's,

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:24.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was your fifth-grade
teacher, Sue Mullen,

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:26.259 line:92%
was elected to state office,

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:30.430
and the first Democrat in
I think over -- since the '40s.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
-85 years.
-85 years.

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:35.034 size:78% position:39% line:92%
To state legislature.

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:37.236 line:92%
-And the first woman ever.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The first woman ever.
Mind-boggling.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:42.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was your
fifth-grade teacher.

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:43.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, Mrs. Mullen.

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you have any
Sue Mullen memories?

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:47.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
I don't remember this,

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.515 line:92%
but she tells this story.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.284 size:75% position:38% line:92%
She, in fifth grade,

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:54.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess asked me what I wanted
to be when I grew up.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:06:00.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said either
a scientist or a lesbian.

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:02.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm actually not attracted
to women personally,

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:06.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I thought it was a job
and it seemed easy.

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:09.869
-That seems like -- Fifth grade
seems old to get that wrong.

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:12.905 line:92%
-I know. It was old, but...

